<ansi fg="black-bold">.:</ansi> <ansi fg="magenta">Help for </ansi><ansi fg="command">beasttamer-routes</ansi>

The Beast Tamer is a neutral lineage. At level 10 it promotes to one of three
classes, and any alignment may choose any of them. Each class chooses the
beast and adds four ranks (10, 15, 20, 25); a talent adds more
(<ansi fg="command">help talents</ansi>). A beast's health below is a share of the starting wolf's.

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">Houndmaster</ansi>

  10 Warhound           your beast is a warhound with 110% of a wolf's health;
                        its bites hobble a foe below half health, who can't
                        flee and moves slowly for a few rounds
  15 Keen nose          +2 Attack on the warhound's bites
  20 Sharp fangs        +1 damage on the warhound's bites
  25 Heavy build        the warhound has 130% of a wolf's health

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">Bearward</ansi>

  10 War bear           your beast is a war bear with 120% of a wolf's health;
                        it steps in and takes a blow meant for the most hurt
                        ally (the Tamer too), three times a battle
  15 Thick hide         +1 damage on the bear's blows
  20 Old bear           the bear has 140% of a wolf's health
  25 Steady guard       the bear guards one more time a battle

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">Dragon Tamer</ansi>

  10 Drake hatchling    your beast is a drake hatchling (a smaller bite, 1d6);
                        every 3 rounds, in place of its bite, it breathes
                        fire on its foe and up to two other foes, 1d6 plus
                        half the Tamer's level in damage to each
  15 Scorching breath   +2 damage on the drake's bites and its Breath
  20 Growing drake      the drake has 120% of a wolf's health
  25 Quick fire         Breath comes every 2 rounds

The elite classes of these routes (Packlord, Beastlord, Dragon Lord) are still
to come; until then a Beast Tamer keeps its advanced class's ranks.

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">Talents</ansi>

Thick Pelt (+10% beast health), Strong Jaws (+1 beast damage), Steady Leash
(Rally one more time, once) and Field Hand (+1 Evasion) suit any route
(<ansi fg="command">help talents</ansi>).

See also: <ansi fg="command">help beasttamer</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help beast</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help classes</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help promotion</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help talents</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help abilities</ansi>.
